As far as the GPL is concerned, NetBSD doesn't, and won't, have GPL'd 
code in the kernel.  In fact, the amount of GPL'd code in the tree is 
kept to a minimum (as much as is feasible).

A mess ... hmm, well, giving it a closer look, it's "neat" in terms of 
whitespace (mostly) and lining things up, etc ... however, at least a 
couple of no-no's caught my eye:

